nodes.body:
@NolenLiang Thanks—your NIXL follow-up and hardware measurements would be welcome. This PR is focused on core sharing with the built-in CPU offloading path; NIXL support isn't currently being implemented here.

Building a separate follow-up against this branch makes sense, with the caveat that the contract may change during maintainer review. NIXL will need explicit compatibility and lease handling, including keeping transfers alive after owner cancellation and releasing every producer-side request.

Please share the cold 1P+1D GRPO baseline: duplicate transfers, transferred bytes, unique destination GPU blocks, and TTFT, together with concurrency, prefix length, model, and TP configuration. That would help establish the benefit and guide validation.

